1
00:02:26,791 --> 00:02:32,125
"Heart Set on Her"

2
00:02:34,593 --> 00:02:36,314
I'm sorry, Mommy Chiu.

3
00:02:36,339 --> 00:02:38,172
It's okay. Hurry and sit down.

4
00:02:39,148 --> 00:02:40,023
Your hair is too messy.

5
00:02:40,048 --> 00:02:40,725
No, it's not.

6
00:02:40,750 --> 00:02:42,875
You think
other people's time isn't important?

7
00:02:48,421 --> 00:02:50,546
Chiu Mommy, this tastes really good.

8
00:02:51,783 --> 00:02:54,236
You eat first. You're very sweet.

9
00:02:54,611 --> 00:02:56,017
You're dressed so beautifully today.

10
00:02:56,042 --> 00:02:57,792
Thank you, Chiu Mommy.

11
00:02:57,817 --> 00:02:59,850
Usually, you refuse to wear
a skirt no matter what.

12
00:02:59,875 --> 00:03:02,220
What's going on now, suddenly volunteering?

13
00:03:02,618 --> 00:03:04,618
Mia is naturally beautiful.

14
00:03:04,643 --> 00:03:06,268
Our families have great genes!

15
00:03:06,293 --> 00:03:09,900
Thanks, but it's too soon
to talk about that.

16
00:03:12,611 --> 00:03:13,267
Mrs. Fang.

17
00:03:13,292 --> 00:03:15,611
Excuse me, she takes my surname.

18
00:03:15,643 --> 00:03:17,783
I'm single, it's Miss Fang.

19
00:03:20,658 --> 00:03:21,876
Miss Fang,

20
00:03:22,884 --> 00:03:27,423
today we're sitting down to discuss
the children's marriage.

21
00:03:27,448 --> 00:03:29,361
Please don't talk like this.

22
00:03:29,900 --> 00:03:31,025
Like what?

23
00:03:32,212 --> 00:03:33,796
Never mind.

24
00:03:44,181 --> 00:03:45,541
Why aren't you letting me eat this?

25
00:03:45,541 --> 00:03:46,908
You can't eat this.

26
00:03:46,933 --> 00:03:47,850
Why not?

27
00:03:47,875 --> 00:03:50,125
Don't you see there are peanuts here?
Can't you smell it?

28
00:03:50,267 --> 00:03:51,634
Where are the peanuts? I didn't see them.

29
00:03:51,659 --> 00:03:53,183
If you eat it,
you'll have an allergic reaction.

30
00:03:53,208 --> 00:03:55,500
You really worry me.

31
00:03:56,281 --> 00:03:58,572
I can't always be there to watch over you.

32
00:04:01,731 --> 00:04:06,775
The kids said traditional marriage
customs aren't popular anymore,

33
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:09,217
and that we don't need a betrothal gift.

34
00:04:09,375 --> 00:04:13,583
Let's just hold a small gathering,
three or five tables, and celebrate together.

35
00:04:13,775 --> 00:04:16,814
I don't care how you arrange the wedding.

36
00:04:16,839 --> 00:04:19,297
But regarding the betrothal gift,
I have the final say.

37
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:24,125
660,000 NTD for the big gift,
160,000 NTD for the small one.

38
00:04:24,697 --> 00:04:26,625
Not a penny less.

39
00:04:26,728 --> 00:04:28,525
But they already agreed it wasn't necessary.

40
00:04:28,550 --> 00:04:32,633
But I just said, I decide
whether the betrothal gift is necessary.

41
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,766
The amount you're talking
about is quite large,

42
00:04:35,791 --> 00:04:37,541
it could burden the kids.

43
00:04:37,541 --> 00:04:41,376
How about our two families split the amount
as a goodwill gesture for them?

44
00:04:42,919 --> 00:04:44,134
They're getting married

45
00:04:45,243 --> 00:04:47,572
the betrothal gift
shouldn't be a problem, right?

46
00:04:48,625 --> 00:04:51,833
Why should my daughter pay a betrothal gift
when both children are getting married?

47
00:04:51,833 --> 00:04:54,625
I'm ensuring my daughter's happiness
for the rest of her life.

48
00:04:57,489 --> 00:04:59,739
Aren't you getting a little carried away?

49
00:04:59,958 --> 00:05:01,250
Let me ask you, then:

50
00:05:01,250 --> 00:05:04,728
Who's responsible for
my daughter's future happiness?

51
00:05:05,166 --> 00:05:08,869
Your daughter's happiness
isn't my responsibility, is it?

52
00:05:14,645 --> 00:05:16,892
Let me ask you, do you have a job?

53
00:05:18,213 --> 00:05:19,392
How much do you make each month?

54
00:05:19,830 --> 00:05:20,673
Oh, I usually do...

55
00:05:20,698 --> 00:05:22,228
Mom, don't ask people questions like that.

56
00:05:22,253 --> 00:05:23,744
I'll handle the betrothal gift.

57
00:05:24,384 --> 00:05:28,400
Hey, I've raised you for thirty years,
and now someone else gets all the benefits?

58
00:05:29,320 --> 00:05:31,158
A betrothal gift is a must.

59
00:05:31,856 --> 00:05:33,913
If there's a gift,
we'll continue discussions.

60
00:05:33,947 --> 00:05:36,572
If not, we'll see about it.

61
00:05:37,033 --> 00:05:39,583
I have something to do,
so I'm leaving first.

62
00:05:39,583 --> 00:05:41,689
Please, take your time.

63
00:06:00,583 --> 00:06:02,458
Good thing you reacted quickly.

64
00:06:02,458 --> 00:06:05,564
If I had known your mom
was allergic to peanuts,

65
00:06:05,589 --> 00:06:07,673
I wouldn't have ordered
the salted egg squid.

66
00:06:07,698 --> 00:06:09,236
Chiu Mommy, don't worry about her.

67
00:06:09,261 --> 00:06:11,427
She's the only one
who can't eat peanuts, not all of us.

68
00:06:11,541 --> 00:06:13,447
Oh right, about the betrothal gift.

69
00:06:13,472 --> 00:06:14,892
Don't worry, I'll handle it myself.

70
00:06:16,153 --> 00:06:18,470
How will you handle it?
It's not a small amount of money.

71
00:06:18,495 --> 00:06:20,673
I'll just work harder, put in more effort.

72
00:06:21,543 --> 00:06:23,072
But how exactly will you do that?

73
00:06:38,791 --> 00:06:40,000
Are you in a bad mood?

74
00:06:41,510 --> 00:06:42,799
What else would it be?

75
00:06:45,458 --> 00:06:46,666
You know it yourself.

76
00:06:53,383 --> 00:06:54,591
Is there really so much love?

77
00:06:55,413 --> 00:06:57,079
Do you absolutely have to get married?

78
00:07:01,939 --> 00:07:03,606
Is getting married a bad thing?

79
00:07:08,929 --> 00:07:11,955
Ahhh! Cockroach! Cockroach!

80
00:07:15,679 --> 00:07:17,494
Over there, over there!

81
00:07:30,916 --> 00:07:32,166
I'm sorry.

82
00:07:32,770 --> 00:07:33,923
What for?

83
00:07:37,515 --> 00:07:38,973
It's about my mom,

84
00:07:39,177 --> 00:07:42,501
insisting on a betrothal gift
for marrying off her daughter.

85
00:07:43,038 --> 00:07:44,204
Why are you apologizing?

86
00:07:46,843 --> 00:07:48,176
She's my mom, so I'll take care of her.

87
00:07:48,201 --> 00:07:51,118
I swear next time
I'll negotiate thoroughly.

88
00:07:53,416 --> 00:07:55,103
Even the betrothal gift?

89
00:07:56,911 --> 00:07:57,970
Of course.

90
00:07:58,283 --> 00:08:00,369
Don't think too much about it;
I'll handle it.

91
00:08:01,372 --> 00:08:03,205
I think you're thinking too little about it.

92
00:08:03,952 --> 00:08:05,314
Look, just one dinner,

93
00:08:05,338 --> 00:08:07,338
and suddenly there’s an extra eight
hundred thousand betrothal gift.

94
00:08:07,916 --> 00:08:10,064
That's not what we agreed upon originally.

95
00:08:10,673 --> 00:08:11,875
Listen, my mom just wants money.

96
00:08:11,875 --> 00:08:13,447
If she wants money, we'll give it to her.

97
00:08:14,687 --> 00:08:16,270
This isn't about money.

98
00:08:18,939 --> 00:08:21,166
Your mom simply doesn't like me.

99
00:08:21,887 --> 00:08:23,603
She doesn't dislike you;

100
00:08:23,973 --> 00:08:26,975
she's just weird.

101
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,072
Let's not worry about her.

102
00:08:28,096 --> 00:08:30,001
After all, marriage is about the two of us.

103
00:08:31,791 --> 00:08:34,041
Dating is just about us being happy,

104
00:08:34,419 --> 00:08:36,377
but marriage involves both families.

105
00:08:37,015 --> 00:08:38,348
Haven't you realized that?

106
00:08:39,345 --> 00:08:40,804
You don't trust me.

107
00:08:43,921 --> 00:08:45,392
What now?

108
00:08:46,718 --> 00:08:48,593
My heart hurts, Your Majesty.

109
00:08:50,103 --> 00:08:51,619
Massage it for me.

110
00:08:51,644 --> 00:08:53,144
Stop messing around.

111
00:08:53,169 --> 00:08:55,720
It hurts right here.

112
00:08:58,856 --> 00:09:02,433
And here, massage here too, Your Majesty.

113
00:09:02,458 --> 00:09:05,208
Stop it, I'm being serious.

114
00:09:05,208 --> 00:09:07,603
Don't be so serious; my heart really hurts,
Your Majesty.

115
00:09:33,439 --> 00:09:34,923
Hello?

116
00:09:36,596 --> 00:09:38,135
I'm busy.

117
00:09:39,478 --> 00:09:41,837
I already told you,
I'm very busy right now.

118
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:45,283
I'm not available.

119
00:09:46,583 --> 00:09:48,833
Wow, it's so beautiful.

120
00:09:48,833 --> 00:09:50,689
I told you
I don't want to wear this type of dress.

121
00:09:50,713 --> 00:09:52,962
Why waste time trying it on?

122
00:09:53,400 --> 00:09:56,173
No, it looks great.

123
00:09:56,197 --> 00:09:57,548
You should try more styles.

124
00:09:57,573 --> 00:09:58,978
It suits you, right?

125
00:09:59,003 --> 00:10:01,836
This is our latest bridal gown this season.

126
00:10:01,861 --> 00:10:02,903
Mom has great taste.

127
00:10:03,788 --> 00:10:05,189
Did you invite him here?

128
00:10:07,481 --> 00:10:10,533
I think your chest
needs a bit more padding, right?

129
00:10:11,020 --> 00:10:12,611
No, I think it looks fine as it is.

130
00:10:12,636 --> 00:10:15,978
I came all the way here
just to hear you discuss my chest?

131
00:10:16,003 --> 00:10:17,236
It's okay, it's okay.

132
00:10:17,260 --> 00:10:19,501
Moms and husbands have different views.

133
00:10:19,526 --> 00:10:20,975
Beauty is in the eye of the beholder, right?

134
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:24,111
Wait, we aren't even together.
Why are you listening to her?

135
00:10:24,483 --> 00:10:26,860
I'm sorry. I'm only here
because your mom asked me to come.

136
00:10:31,250 --> 00:10:33,791
Ah, is this your younger sister?

137
00:10:33,791 --> 00:10:37,236
She's as beautiful as her older sister.

138
00:10:37,261 --> 00:10:39,158
Does the dress suit your sister?

139
00:10:40,439 --> 00:10:42,898
This latest mermaid-style bridal gown
is so fitted and stunning.

140
00:10:43,191 --> 00:10:45,399
Wow, gorgeous!

141
00:10:48,484 --> 00:10:50,234
It's okay.

142
00:10:56,921 --> 00:10:59,001
I'm really not in contact with him anymore.

143
00:10:59,942 --> 00:11:01,212
I know.

144
00:11:11,250 --> 00:11:12,853
Are you really not mad?

145
00:11:13,390 --> 00:11:14,759
No, I'm not.

146
00:11:16,333 --> 00:11:17,416
Really?

147
00:11:19,500 --> 00:11:22,208
Really, I'm not.

148
00:11:34,067 --> 00:11:35,900
You're really not going to fix your scooter?

149
00:11:36,041 --> 00:11:37,283
No need.

150
00:11:37,664 --> 00:11:39,431
I've ridden this old scooter
for over ten years;

151
00:11:39,455 --> 00:11:40,384
it's worth its value.

152
00:11:41,064 --> 00:11:42,750
Then will you get a new one?

153
00:11:42,775 --> 00:11:43,876
Nope.

154
00:11:45,184 --> 00:11:47,712
I want to spend the money
on our wedding instead.

155
00:11:49,884 --> 00:11:52,176
See? There's no problem.

156
00:12:15,035 --> 00:12:16,077
Hello?

157
00:12:16,900 --> 00:12:20,673
I forgot the safe's password.
Can you tell me?

158
00:12:21,403 --> 00:12:24,298
Why can't you remember your own password?

159
00:12:24,322 --> 00:12:26,040
It's 19700807.

160
00:12:26,065 --> 00:12:27,065
Wait, wait.

161
00:12:27,322 --> 00:12:30,111
Bring me a box of tissues
when you come home today.

162
00:12:31,008 --> 00:12:33,799
I'm not coming home today.

163
00:12:34,337 --> 00:12:37,129
I need to use the bathroom.
How can I do that without tissues?

164
00:12:37,863 --> 00:12:39,814
If you're out of tissues, go downstairs.

165
00:12:39,838 --> 00:12:41,226
There's a 7-Eleven downstairs, isn't there?

166
00:12:41,250 --> 00:12:43,416
If you're too lazy to go out,
just rinse with water. Bye!

167
00:12:49,187 --> 00:12:50,687
You're drawing me?

168
00:12:53,046 --> 00:12:54,254
Wait, you haven't drawn for a long time.

169
00:12:54,601 --> 00:12:57,642
Yeah, a senior offered me a project.

170
00:12:58,062 --> 00:12:59,103
Is the pay good?

171
00:13:01,666 --> 00:13:06,447
I mean, if it's too low,
you shouldn't accept it,

172
00:13:06,471 --> 00:13:07,869
or you'll get exhausted.

173
00:13:09,025 --> 00:13:11,150
Who am I to be picky about projects?

174
00:13:15,333 --> 00:13:16,333
I'm coming in.

175
00:13:16,333 --> 00:13:17,837
Oh, Chiu Mommy.

176
00:13:18,822 --> 00:13:20,143
Chiu Mommy.

177
00:13:23,208 --> 00:13:25,290
Here, this is a small gesture from me.

178
00:13:25,720 --> 00:13:28,305
It's the deposit Ah Ming
and I had saved before.

179
00:13:28,330 --> 00:13:29,875
Use it to help cover the betrothal gift.

180
00:13:29,875 --> 00:13:31,728
Otherwise, it'll be too hard on you both.

181
00:13:31,986 --> 00:13:34,083
Auntie, there's no need.
I'll figure it out myself.

182
00:13:34,083 --> 00:13:35,875
Come on,
your happiness is what matters most.

183
00:13:35,875 --> 00:13:37,439
Money can always be earned again.

184
00:13:38,187 --> 00:13:39,720
Just accept it,

185
00:13:40,752 --> 00:13:43,697
so our Emma won't be looked down
upon by your mom.

186
00:13:43,747 --> 00:13:46,080
What nonsense are you talking about?

187
00:13:46,463 --> 00:13:49,580
Stop it.

188
00:13:51,166 --> 00:13:53,439
Why bring this up now?

189
00:13:54,083 --> 00:13:57,134
What does she mean by "taking responsibility
for her daughter's happiness"?

190
00:14:11,416 --> 00:14:13,291
Do you feel the same way?

191
00:14:15,174 --> 00:14:16,361
No,

192
00:14:17,205 --> 00:14:19,393
that's just their opinion.

193
00:14:19,845 --> 00:14:22,345
Everyone defines happiness differently.

194
00:14:24,735 --> 00:14:27,103
I'm very happy when I'm with you.

195
00:14:29,375 --> 00:14:32,189
But after deciding to marry,

196
00:14:33,346 --> 00:14:34,986
I don't know,

197
00:14:36,103 --> 00:14:38,353
it feels like
there are so many tasks to complete.

198
00:14:40,793 --> 00:14:42,337
Sometimes I'm lost.

199
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:45,845
It seems life has become all about
gathering money for the betrothal gift.

200
00:14:57,611 --> 00:14:59,525
You misunderstood me.

201
00:15:00,251 --> 00:15:02,283
You're concerned about money right now, right?

202
00:15:02,307 --> 00:15:04,165
Then I'll just go and solve it.

203
00:15:08,716 --> 00:15:10,634
Sorry, sorry.

204
00:15:11,708 --> 00:15:13,791
But won't your mom dislike me
even more if you do this?

205
00:15:13,791 --> 00:15:14,845
Don't worry about her.

206
00:15:14,869 --> 00:15:16,517
If the betrothal gift is solved,
won't you be happy?

207
00:15:16,541 --> 00:15:17,541
No, I won't be happy.

208
00:15:17,541 --> 00:15:18,541
Why?

209
00:15:18,853 --> 00:15:20,208
I'll feel guilty.

210
00:15:21,040 --> 00:15:22,955
I pawned it, not sold it.

211
00:15:22,980 --> 00:15:24,462
We can redeem it later.

212
00:15:24,641 --> 00:15:26,641
The important thing is that
we can get married smoothly.

213
00:15:26,666 --> 00:15:28,744
You'll be happy, and so will I.

214
00:15:31,064 --> 00:15:32,798
Then how will you redeem it?

215
00:15:34,020 --> 00:15:37,580
Do you know how to make the masters
want to buy your Polaroids?

216
00:15:39,710 --> 00:15:42,501
Make the masters happy.

217
00:15:43,632 --> 00:15:45,007
Go ahead.

218
00:16:03,955 --> 00:16:06,539
Woof woof, meow meow,

219
00:16:07,333 --> 00:16:08,833
moe moe,

220
00:16:12,080 --> 00:16:15,837
wow, oishii, food tastes good,

221
00:16:19,070 --> 00:16:21,283
yeah, the food is tasty now!

222
00:16:24,617 --> 00:16:26,075
Can we take a picture?

223
00:16:28,548 --> 00:16:30,861
Let's pose with hearts on our cheeks.

224
00:16:42,165 --> 00:16:44,064
Thank you.

225
00:16:46,041 --> 00:16:48,208
One more? OK.

226
00:16:52,590 --> 00:16:56,384
Moe moe

227
00:16:56,749 --> 00:17:01,369
oishiku nare.

228
00:17:04,985 --> 00:17:06,345
How much do you make per photo?

229
00:17:06,726 --> 00:17:07,892
Two hundred.

230
00:17:09,676 --> 00:17:11,468
How many photos did you take today?

231
00:17:12,837 --> 00:17:14,296
None.

232
00:17:16,465 --> 00:17:17,915
Why?

233
00:17:19,351 --> 00:17:21,345
Because the masters weren't happy.

234
00:17:22,437 --> 00:17:27,770
Then how do you make the masters happy?

235
00:17:29,142 --> 00:17:32,892
Master, you're so beautiful!

236
00:17:33,259 --> 00:17:37,400
Whatever you want Mia to do,
Mia is OK with it.

237
00:17:38,129 --> 00:17:42,736
Then I want Mia to tell
her first love story.

238
00:17:43,244 --> 00:17:46,001
Mia's first love is you.

239
00:17:47,728 --> 00:17:49,016
Oh, stop it.

240
00:17:49,041 --> 00:17:51,166
Let's take a picture,
I'll only charge you one hundred.

241
00:17:51,166 --> 00:17:52,833
Who earns money like that?

242
00:17:52,833 --> 00:17:55,000
You meow, or I meow.

243
00:17:55,275 --> 00:17:59,931
No, you meow and I'll woof.
Alright, ready, one two three—

244
00:18:00,049 --> 00:18:01,658
(Mommy)

245
00:18:03,465 --> 00:18:08,126
One more time. You meow, I woof.
One two three...

246
00:18:08,151 --> 00:18:09,205
(Mommy)

247
00:18:15,429 --> 00:18:16,804
Aren't you going to call back?

248
00:18:20,497 --> 00:18:22,622
It might be something important.

249
00:18:56,821 --> 00:18:58,238
Mom, I'm home!

250
00:19:02,931 --> 00:19:04,348
Mom, I'm back.

251
00:19:20,049 --> 00:19:23,174
Where did you go?
You asked me to come back, you...

252
00:19:28,416 --> 00:19:29,798
Come in.

253
00:19:32,624 --> 00:19:34,665
I just brought Auntie home, nothing else.

254
00:19:36,473 --> 00:19:38,806
You don't need a reason
to come to Auntie's home.

255
00:19:38,831 --> 00:19:40,206
Come in and sit down.

256
00:19:42,273 --> 00:19:43,648
I'll take it.

257
00:19:45,125 --> 00:19:46,775
Auntie twisted her hand
moving things earlier.

258
00:19:46,799 --> 00:19:48,189
Luckily, no bones were hurt.

259
00:19:48,509 --> 00:19:50,220
The doctor said she'll be fine
after resting.

260
00:19:51,416 --> 00:19:54,658
It's okay, Auntie. I'll be leaving now.

261
00:19:55,208 --> 00:19:57,523
Okay. Jia Hao, thank you.

262
00:19:57,548 --> 00:19:59,047
You're welcome. Auntie, just call me
if you need anything else.

263
00:19:59,072 --> 00:20:00,758
Be careful on your way.

264
00:20:07,020 --> 00:20:09,791
Are you hungry? I'll make you some noodles.

265
00:20:10,742 --> 00:20:13,290
I didn't know your hand was hurt.
I'm sorry.

266
00:20:13,323 --> 00:20:15,595
I thought you were like last time.

267
00:20:18,375 --> 00:20:19,125
I'll move it.

268
00:20:19,125 --> 00:20:21,666
No need, I'll do it myself.

269
00:20:24,583 --> 00:20:30,533
It'd be nice if Jia Hao could be my godson.

270
00:20:30,558 --> 00:20:33,970
A son-in-law is like half a son anyway,
so it's about the same.

271
00:20:35,208 --> 00:20:38,500
I haven't talked to him about it yet.
I'm not sure if he'll agree.

272
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:41,267
You keep talking about Jia Hao.

273
00:20:41,292 --> 00:20:42,225
Why don't you just be with him then?

274
00:20:42,250 --> 00:20:44,041
What nonsense are you talking about?

275
00:20:44,375 --> 00:20:47,333
He was deeply hurt because of you.

276
00:20:47,836 --> 00:20:49,752
I'm just making amends for you, okay?

277
00:20:49,777 --> 00:20:51,455
Making amends for what?

278
00:20:51,479 --> 00:20:53,103
You think I've never been hurt?

279
00:20:53,512 --> 00:20:55,759
Miss, what injury did you have? Huh?

280
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:59,228
You weren't hurt.
You do whatever you want anyway.

281
00:20:59,525 --> 00:21:01,650
Do you even care what I say?

282
00:21:02,570 --> 00:21:05,580
And you're always running off
to someone else's house.

283
00:21:06,166 --> 00:21:08,908
How many days a week
do you actually live here?

284
00:21:10,142 --> 00:21:11,845
Having a daughter is a loss for me.

285
00:21:11,870 --> 00:21:17,095
Other people have kids—having a daughter
means gaining another daughter. How nice.

286
00:21:17,595 --> 00:21:18,947
Don't worry.

287
00:21:18,971 --> 00:21:21,345
The big gift is sixty-six,
the small gift sixteen—

288
00:21:21,407 --> 00:21:23,509
I'll give it to you on that day,
not one bill short.

289
00:21:23,533 --> 00:21:24,697
Is that good enough?

290
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:26,330
What is this?

291
00:21:27,010 --> 00:21:28,766
Are you trying to throw money at me?

292
00:21:28,791 --> 00:21:30,267
I've given you all my best things—

293
00:21:30,291 --> 00:21:32,978
even that necklace,
my most important necklace.

294
00:21:33,369 --> 00:21:35,369
Is this how you repay me?

295
00:21:38,970 --> 00:21:40,208
Where's your necklace?

296
00:21:40,625 --> 00:21:42,791
Where did it go? The necklace!

297
00:21:42,978 --> 00:21:45,462
What's wrong with you? I just put it away.

298
00:21:45,833 --> 00:21:48,244
Where did you put it?
Tell me exactly where!

299
00:21:48,269 --> 00:21:50,322
I told you, I put it away.
What exactly do you want?

300
00:21:54,236 --> 00:21:56,400
You mentioned the deposit.
Where is the money?

301
00:21:56,830 --> 00:21:58,345
Emma's family will provide it.

302
00:21:58,370 --> 00:21:59,494
Don't lie to me.

303
00:21:59,518 --> 00:22:01,197
What do you mean they'll provide it?

304
00:22:02,375 --> 00:22:04,541
Hey, why don't you trust me at all?

305
00:22:04,541 --> 00:22:06,111
Trust you about what?

306
00:22:06,135 --> 00:22:08,416
Trust you for attending that lousy school?

307
00:22:08,441 --> 00:22:10,455
I have a job.
Have I ever asked you for money?

308
00:22:10,480 --> 00:22:12,688
Don't even mention that lousy job.

309
00:22:12,713 --> 00:22:16,009
You know I'm embarrassed to tell people
where my daughter works.

310
00:22:16,034 --> 00:22:17,587
Then stop telling others
you have a daughter!

311
00:22:17,612 --> 00:22:19,283
Let me tell you, I pawned the necklace too.

312
00:22:29,504 --> 00:22:32,129
You refused the wedding dress I chose.

313
00:22:32,923 --> 00:22:35,632
You rejected the good boy I liked.

314
00:22:37,807 --> 00:22:38,948
Now

315
00:22:40,323 --> 00:22:43,846
I've given you
my most precious birthday gift,

316
00:22:44,745 --> 00:22:46,268
and you don't even care.

317
00:22:47,259 --> 00:22:49,001
Do you realize how valuable that necklace is?

318
00:22:49,026 --> 00:22:51,401
It could be a family heirloom!

319
00:22:51,541 --> 00:22:55,750
Exactly. Because it was so important,
I pawned it to get the cash you demanded.

320
00:22:58,208 --> 00:23:01,166
You're really something, aren't you?

321
00:23:01,487 --> 00:23:04,916
How could you pawn the necklace I gave you
and give me the money?

322
00:23:20,416 --> 00:23:21,375
Fine.

323
00:23:23,398 --> 00:23:25,987
I'll still attend your wedding.

324
00:23:28,431 --> 00:23:31,604
But please move out of this place,
move out of this house.

325
00:23:31,628 --> 00:23:33,932
You hardly come home anyway.

326
00:23:35,067 --> 00:23:39,830
I'll be just fine alone, even without you.

327
00:23:41,322 --> 00:23:43,989
Don't you ever wonder
why I don't want to come home?

328
00:23:44,946 --> 00:23:47,613
It's because you always make me
feel worthless and useless.

329
00:24:16,114 --> 00:24:16,989
Listen,

330
00:24:17,778 --> 00:24:19,903
your second aunt and younger uncle
aren't getting along.

331
00:24:20,414 --> 00:24:21,850
Don’t seat them at the same table.

332
00:24:21,875 --> 00:24:22,625
Okay.

333
00:24:24,619 --> 00:24:27,891
Also, your older cousin just gave birth.

334
00:24:27,916 --> 00:24:29,583
She's still recovering
and can't catch cold.

335
00:24:29,890 --> 00:24:31,390
Don't let her sit
under the air conditioner.

336
00:24:32,009 --> 00:24:35,468
Remember to ask where the AC vents are
in the private room.

337
00:24:37,291 --> 00:24:41,916
Oh yeah, didn't you say
Auntie is into some new trend lately?

338
00:24:41,941 --> 00:24:43,558
What was it—“mi-gen” or something?

339
00:24:43,583 --> 00:24:46,708
Vegan! She's vegetarian.

340
00:24:49,875 --> 00:24:51,208
One more thing—

341
00:24:52,625 --> 00:24:55,565
Miss Fang, seat her farther away,

342
00:24:55,924 --> 00:24:58,291
or I'll lose my appetite
as soon as she opens her mouth.

343
00:24:58,291 --> 00:25:00,104
You're talking nonsense again.

344
00:25:00,129 --> 00:25:01,455
Am not!

345
00:25:02,003 --> 00:25:04,987
Can anyone even stand what she says
when she starts talking?

346
00:25:07,250 --> 00:25:09,659
Even if the whole wedding is a disaster,

347
00:25:09,684 --> 00:25:11,308
we can just register our marriage.
That's enough.

348
00:25:11,333 --> 00:25:13,166
That's not what Dad meant.

349
00:25:13,166 --> 00:25:15,166
But he keeps going on and on.

350
00:25:17,940 --> 00:25:19,252
I'm going to take a shower first.

351
00:25:19,277 --> 00:25:20,152
Okay.

352
00:25:31,379 --> 00:25:32,971
She and her mom are exactly the same.

353
00:25:33,875 --> 00:25:35,333
I could tell right away.

354
00:25:36,351 --> 00:25:39,174
You're an outsider—you can't deal with that.

355
00:25:40,750 --> 00:25:42,596
Mia is trying really hard.

356
00:25:42,796 --> 00:25:44,729
She's helping with the betrothal money too.

357
00:25:45,762 --> 00:25:47,479
Didn’t you hear what her mom said?

358
00:25:47,503 --> 00:25:48,901
The daughter doesn't even dare talk back.

359
00:25:50,372 --> 00:25:51,914
Now it's about betrothal money.

360
00:25:52,916 --> 00:25:53,791
What about later—

361
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:56,799
when they demand a son
or to carry on the family name?

362
00:25:56,823 --> 00:25:57,987
What will you do then?

363
00:25:58,539 --> 00:26:01,330
Okay, okay, just stop talking for now.

364
00:26:11,546 --> 00:26:14,252
If she's willing to follow
her mom's words and date a guy,

365
00:26:15,206 --> 00:26:16,698
then what else is impossible?

366
00:26:18,500 --> 00:26:23,768
You, still insisting on marrying her
like a fool,

367
00:26:24,970 --> 00:26:27,526
just don't come crying home again
like last time.

368
00:26:33,957 --> 00:26:35,166
Dad,

369
00:26:36,378 --> 00:26:39,565
I already booked the restaurant
and sent out the invitations.

370
00:26:39,856 --> 00:26:41,916
Why bring up the past now?

371
00:26:42,583 --> 00:26:44,096
I'm doing this for you…

372
00:27:27,939 --> 00:27:30,291
I didn't even finish
what I wanted to say.

373
00:27:32,583 --> 00:27:38,083
If you really don't want to get married,
you can just tell me directly.

374
00:27:38,763 --> 00:27:42,013
Everything's already set,
the invitations are sent.

375
00:27:42,666 --> 00:27:44,375
Why bring up the past?

376
00:27:47,062 --> 00:27:48,520
Come on!

377
00:27:52,041 --> 00:27:55,416
I just want to marry the person
I love most!

378
00:27:56,583 --> 00:27:59,798
Did you not hear the point?
And you're over here crying secretly.

379
00:28:02,922 --> 00:28:05,869
I don't have a car,
or a house, I have nothing.

380
00:28:05,893 --> 00:28:07,619
I don't even have any real skills.

381
00:28:08,625 --> 00:28:12,080
But you have me.

382
00:28:13,627 --> 00:28:17,127
And who says you need a car
or a house to be happy?

383
00:28:18,000 --> 00:28:19,798
We have each other,

384
00:28:22,104 --> 00:28:23,174
right?

385
00:28:23,931 --> 00:28:27,611
Then why didn't you say that earlier?
You're so annoying!

386
00:28:29,583 --> 00:28:32,208
We'll get married. We'll work hard.

387
00:28:32,580 --> 00:28:34,414
I'm trying hard too.

388
00:28:57,908 --> 00:28:58,700
Here's your meal.

389
00:28:58,725 --> 00:28:59,548
Thank you.

390
00:28:59,573 --> 00:29:00,283
Enjoy your meal.

391
00:29:00,308 --> 00:29:00,970
Thank you.

392
00:29:10,750 --> 00:29:14,666
Oishiku nare~ Q!

393
00:29:18,666 --> 00:29:19,958
Thank you, Master.

394
00:29:32,056 --> 00:29:34,000
We should've brought fishing rods.

395
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:35,541
We could've fished here.

396
00:29:40,228 --> 00:29:42,189
Hey, we're getting married in a few days!

397
00:29:42,214 --> 00:29:43,089
Mhm.

398
00:29:43,125 --> 00:29:44,416
Aren't you nervous?

399
00:29:44,441 --> 00:29:46,697
Nope. What's there to be nervous about?

400
00:29:48,000 --> 00:29:49,181
I'm super nervous.

401
00:29:49,206 --> 00:29:51,331
Why are you nervous? You're so beautiful.

402
00:29:52,338 --> 00:29:54,088
Just thinking about wearing
that wedding dress…

403
00:29:54,113 --> 00:29:56,322
It's great!
It'll show off your amazing figure.

404
00:29:56,375 --> 00:29:57,583
I'm saying this now—

405
00:29:57,583 --> 00:30:00,470
this is a big banquet, lots of people.

406
00:30:00,587 --> 00:30:03,291
You're going to give the speech
and do the toasts first!

407
00:30:03,291 --> 00:30:06,291
Nah, your dad will totally speak.

408
00:30:06,291 --> 00:30:07,642
My dad, your dad.

409
00:30:08,141 --> 00:30:08,932
Whose dad?

410
00:30:08,957 --> 00:30:09,749
My dad.

411
00:30:32,166 --> 00:30:32,958
What?

412
00:30:34,205 --> 00:30:35,330
Are you hungry or something?

413
00:30:35,355 --> 00:30:36,355
Mhm.

414
00:30:36,380 --> 00:30:38,281
What do you wanna eat?

415
00:30:39,791 --> 00:30:40,708
You know what I want.

416
00:30:41,625 --> 00:30:42,541
No, I don't!

417
00:30:42,541 --> 00:30:43,708
You do know.

418
00:30:43,708 --> 00:30:44,828
No, I don't!

419
00:30:49,041 --> 00:30:50,726
Don't copy me!

420
00:30:50,751 --> 00:30:52,001
Ugh, you're so annoying!

421
00:31:25,291 --> 00:31:26,083
Auntie.

422
00:31:26,446 --> 00:31:28,031
I only have five minutes.

423
00:31:28,614 --> 00:31:30,953
Okay, then please have a seat first.

424
00:31:36,352 --> 00:31:38,055
I edited this video myself.

425
00:31:38,392 --> 00:31:41,070
I wanted to show it as a surprise
at our wedding,

426
00:31:42,395 --> 00:31:44,476
but I felt you should see it first.

427
00:31:48,416 --> 00:31:49,958
Baby, what’s your favorite food?

428
00:31:49,958 --> 00:31:56,211
Little pumpkin! Pump-pump-pump—
pump your head!

429
00:31:57,250 --> 00:32:00,208
Our Mia is so adorable.

430
00:32:04,125 --> 00:32:06,458
I'm worried Mommy will catch a cold.

431
00:32:06,458 --> 00:32:07,833
It's okay, Mommy. No more pain now.

432
00:32:07,833 --> 00:32:11,000
I'm worried Mommy will catch a cold.

433
00:32:12,166 --> 00:32:14,458
Mommy, I like your necklace.

434
00:32:14,458 --> 00:32:17,708
When you grow up,
Mommy will give it to you, okay?

435
00:32:21,333 --> 00:32:22,476
And then?

436
00:32:23,461 --> 00:32:25,329
After growing up, she left me.

437
00:32:26,708 --> 00:32:31,750
No, that's not it.
Mia really misses you and feels guilty.

438
00:32:32,293 --> 00:32:34,418
She's just working really hard right now.

439
00:32:35,578 --> 00:32:39,016
Yeah, running around
doing deliveries like crazy.

440
00:32:41,208 --> 00:32:44,958
Auntie, Mia's working so hard—

441
00:32:45,215 --> 00:32:48,859
not to prove she's grown up
or that she can leave you.

442
00:32:49,973 --> 00:32:52,390
What she really cares about is
how you see her.

443
00:32:54,083 --> 00:32:57,958
All along, she's just been trying
to earn your approval.

444
00:32:58,416 --> 00:33:04,000
Auntie, don't you want to see
what Mia looks like when she's working?

445
00:33:08,411 --> 00:33:10,773
Okay—3, 2, 1!

446
00:33:29,875 --> 00:33:30,875
Thank you.

447
00:33:31,875 --> 00:33:32,875
Excuse me.

448
00:33:39,273 --> 00:33:41,430
Alright—3, 2, 1!

449
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:47,708
What a beautiful and lucky bride!

450
00:33:47,708 --> 00:33:50,333
Wishing the whole family peace
and prosperity.

451
00:33:50,333 --> 00:33:53,625
Pass the tea cup—blessings will follow.

452
00:33:53,625 --> 00:33:55,750
Now, serve tea to your parents.

453
00:33:56,375 --> 00:33:57,916
Dad, Mom, please have some tea.

454
00:34:03,291 --> 00:34:05,166
Sweet tea brings sweet days.

455
00:34:05,166 --> 00:34:08,148
May everyone smile together forever.

456
00:34:15,372 --> 00:34:16,766
With this deep tea cup,

457
00:34:16,790 --> 00:34:20,195
Dad and I wish you two a lifetime
of love and unity as wives.

458
00:34:20,426 --> 00:34:21,648
Thank you, Chiu Mommy.

459
00:34:22,125 --> 00:34:24,719
Now it's Emma's turn to serve tea to Mom.

460
00:34:29,720 --> 00:34:31,095
Don't call me Mom.

461
00:34:33,038 --> 00:34:35,211
I couldn't even raise my own daughter right.

462
00:34:36,004 --> 00:34:38,379
I don't have the kind of luck
to deserve a second one.

463
00:34:44,125 --> 00:34:46,250
Today's a joyful day!

464
00:34:46,520 --> 00:34:49,961
Emma and Mia are getting engaged
and exchanging rings.

465
00:34:49,986 --> 00:34:51,914
Let's all be happy.

466
00:34:53,239 --> 00:34:57,867
Wear the ring just right,
and you'll be cherished forever.

467
00:34:59,625 --> 00:35:01,500
Now Mia, put the ring on Emma.

468
00:35:04,871 --> 00:35:08,937
Bend your finger a little
so it doesn't get pushed all the way down.

469
00:35:12,583 --> 00:35:16,708
The rings are on—time for a family photo!

470
00:35:16,733 --> 00:35:18,117
Wait, wait!

471
00:35:29,666 --> 00:35:32,541
Come on, parents, step in closer.

472
00:35:33,208 --> 00:35:35,375
Smile! 3, 2, 1…

473
00:35:36,273 --> 00:35:38,055
very good! Let's do one more!

474
00:35:38,743 --> 00:35:41,035
What's your most unforgettable
childhood memory?

475
00:35:43,601 --> 00:35:46,476
Probably kindergarten—
my first love confession got rejected.

476
00:35:47,148 --> 00:35:48,508
Was it a boy or a girl?

477
00:35:49,863 --> 00:35:51,530
A girl, of course.

478
00:35:52,708 --> 00:35:55,734
I was so heartbroken back then.

479
00:35:55,947 --> 00:36:00,364
So my mom baked a cake to cheer me up.

480
00:36:00,389 --> 00:36:01,078
The funny part is,

481
00:36:01,102 --> 00:36:02,726
she didn't even know the difference between
all-purpose and cake flour.

482
00:36:02,750 --> 00:36:03,708
So extra!

483
00:36:03,708 --> 00:36:06,375
But that afternoon, I was really happy.

484
00:36:07,708 --> 00:36:10,414
It was the first time
my mom took a day off,

485
00:36:11,708 --> 00:36:13,875
just for me
and spent the whole day with me.

486
00:36:13,875 --> 00:36:15,500
I felt so loved.

487
00:36:21,333 --> 00:36:23,958
Hey, what are you doing?

488
00:36:29,416 --> 00:36:31,766
Dad Ah Ming, Chiu Mommy,

489
00:36:32,907 --> 00:36:35,235
I truly, truly love Emma.

490
00:36:35,536 --> 00:36:38,695
I know I haven't done everything right,

491
00:36:39,282 --> 00:36:40,449
but please trust me—

492
00:36:40,833 --> 00:36:42,916
I will take care of her with all I have.

493
00:36:43,653 --> 00:36:46,945
Even when we're old and can't walk anymore,

494
00:36:47,371 --> 00:36:51,078
I'll still treat her
like my little princess,

495
00:36:51,406 --> 00:36:53,703
protect her, and be there for her.

496
00:36:58,916 --> 00:37:00,666
Okay okay, that's enough now.

497
00:37:00,691 --> 00:37:03,617
I’m gonna kiss you! Nooo—come onnn.

498
00:37:19,840 --> 00:37:25,548
How can two girls be happy together?

499
00:37:26,992 --> 00:37:29,492
Her mom only cares about making money.

500
00:37:29,625 --> 00:37:31,375
Never even paid attention to her kid.

501
00:37:35,168 --> 00:37:38,367
Mia has known who she is
since she was little.

502
00:37:38,391 --> 00:37:39,906
That's a good thing.

503
00:37:47,333 --> 00:37:50,289
Uncle, you're really amazing—
my mom does love making money.

504
00:37:50,314 --> 00:37:51,898
She's basically money-obsessed!

505
00:37:51,923 --> 00:37:55,132
But I heard you failed the college
entrance exam three times.

506
00:37:55,414 --> 00:37:57,708
You just barely crawled
into some no-name school.

507
00:37:57,708 --> 00:38:01,000
Grandpa was so mad
he didn't even talk to you,

508
00:38:01,000 --> 00:38:03,333
and it was my mom who paid your tuition.

509
00:38:04,010 --> 00:38:07,562
Oh right, and every time you got divorced?

510
00:38:07,791 --> 00:38:09,047
Mom paid the alimony.

511
00:38:09,072 --> 00:38:11,092
No wonder she works so hard,

512
00:38:11,117 --> 00:38:12,625
she's busy supporting the whole family.

513
00:38:12,625 --> 00:38:15,291
And you've taken so much money from her,
yet you have the nerve to say that?

514
00:38:15,541 --> 00:38:17,541
My uncle is unbelievably shameless.

515
00:38:18,322 --> 00:38:19,656
Hey, are you done?

516
00:38:19,681 --> 00:38:22,472
I even gave a red envelope.
I didn’t come here to be humiliated by you!

517
00:38:22,516 --> 00:38:26,141
I only came cause your family
doesn't even have a man around.

518
00:38:26,166 --> 00:38:28,000
Kindness gets punished, I swear.

519
00:38:28,583 --> 00:38:30,583
Are you done yet?
You're just here to stir things up?

520
00:38:30,583 --> 00:38:31,891
So rude.

521
00:38:31,916 --> 00:38:34,100
It's just one time.
Let it go, and it'll pass.

522
00:38:34,125 --> 00:38:37,791
Whether it's one time or not—who knows?

523
00:38:38,750 --> 00:38:41,958
Yeah yeah, like you're the expert on marriage!

524
00:38:43,231 --> 00:38:46,195
Because of you, Mia has no aunt,

525
00:38:46,219 --> 00:38:48,609
ex-aunt, ex-ex-aunt, ex-ex-ex-aunt!

526
00:38:48,924 --> 00:38:50,984
I sent out wedding invites

527
00:38:51,531 --> 00:38:52,725
and no one even came.

528
00:38:52,750 --> 00:38:54,166
Everyone hates you!

529
00:38:56,291 --> 00:38:59,750
Sis, you really had to embarrass me
in front of everyone?

530
00:39:01,000 --> 00:39:04,333
Shut up! Sorry everyone, he's drunk.

531
00:39:04,333 --> 00:39:05,791
Let's go.

532
00:39:06,375 --> 00:39:07,791
Am I wrong though?

533
00:39:07,791 --> 00:39:10,208
Just shut up already—
everyone, enjoy the food!

534
00:39:14,708 --> 00:39:16,666
Come on, have a drink.

535
00:39:43,867 --> 00:39:45,158
Mom!

536
00:39:58,208 --> 00:40:00,208
There'll be plenty more times in life
you'll need money.

537
00:40:00,916 --> 00:40:03,291
Mom, thank you.

538
00:40:05,333 --> 00:40:07,041
Remember to come home often.

539
00:40:38,414 --> 00:40:39,942
Did you not eat anything just now?

540
00:40:39,967 --> 00:40:42,050
I couldn't eat at all. I was too nervous.

541
00:40:42,335 --> 00:40:43,585
You didn't eat either, did you?

542
00:40:44,023 --> 00:40:45,106
Then let's go grab some late-night snacks.

543
00:40:45,131 --> 00:40:45,964
Sounds good.

544
00:40:50,924 --> 00:40:59,059
"Heart Set on Her"

